   "source": [
    "# 14. DNS SPOOFING"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "4e0b5ec3-1401-47a6-8984-455ab02e0be4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "DNS (Domain Name System) converts a domain name into\n",
    "an IP address.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "example.com\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "192.0.2.10\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "1. DNS SPOOFING\n",
    "\n",
    "DNS spoofing occurs when an attacker causes a domain name\n",
    "to resolve to an incorrect or attacker-controlled IP address.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "User requests:\n",
    "    example.com\n",
    "\n",
    "Expected:\n",
    "    example.com → 192.0.2.10\n",
    "\n",
    "Attacker causes:\n",
    "    example.com → 203.0.113.50\n",
    "                    ↑\n",
    "              Wrong IP address\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "2. EFFECT\n",
    "\n",
    "The user may be redirected to a malicious server\n",
    "while believing they are communicating with the\n",
    "correct website.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "3. DNS CACHE AND TTL\n",
    "\n",
    "DNS results may be stored (cached) for a specific period.\n",
    "\n",
    "TTL (Time To Live)\n",
    "    → tells how long the DNS result can be cached.\n",
    "\n",
    "After the TTL expires, the DNS information should\n",
    "be refreshed.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "MEMORY TRICK\n",
    "\n",
    "DNS        → Domain name → IP address\n",
    "Spoofing   → Wrong/fake DNS mapping\n",
    "TTL        → How long the mapping can be cached"
   ]
  }
 ],
